TITLE: The Effects of Interval Sprint Training on Physical Performance and Competition Anxiety in College Soccer Players: A Randomized Controlled Trial
SUMMARY: To investigate the comprehensive effects of structured repeated sprint training (RST) on the multidimensional physical performance and competition-related anxiety of college soccer players.
INCLUSION_CRITERIA: 1. Age 18-24 years;
2. At least 3 years of systematic soccer training;
3. No history of severe lower-limb sports injuries within the past 6 months (defined as injuries resulting in ≥4 weeks of training cessation);
4. No participation in any form of repeated sprinting or high-intensity interval training programs during the 2 months prior to the study.

